{
  "title": "Blog fallback keeps a bold sub-recipe heading at the top of the first ingredient list as an ingredient",
  "description": "When an unstructured blog post's recipe title sits in a preceding bold paragraph and the first ingredient `<p>` opens with a different bold component heading, that heading stays an ingredient. \
Example: bakingbites.com 'Peanut Butter Sandwich Cookies with Chocolate Peanut Butter Ganache' has `<p><em><strong> Crispy Salted Peanut Butter Cookies</strong></em><br />1 1/4 cups all purpose flour…`, so 'Crispy Salted Peanut Butter Cookies' appears in data/unique-ingredients.txt. leading_bold_section_title (ramekin-core/src/extract/blog.rs) only promotes a first-list Title-Case bold line when detect_section_header accepts it as written, to avoid swallowing bold ingredients like 'Fresh Parsley'. \
Possible signal: the first block already has a title from a preceding bold paragraph and the later lists in the post also open with bold Title-Case headings (the ganache), so the first list is one component among several.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
